  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Waste management mission to the Netherlands 2017</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to improve the waste sector&apos;s impact in Ghana, help companies expand and improve their services and enable them to cooperate more with programs and projects of the embassy in Ghana and the RVO trade promotion instruments. During a trip to the Netherlands, Ghanaian waste management companies are introduced to the Dutch waste management industry. That helps to foster trade relations and gain knowledge about effective waste management practices and modern recycling technologies. The missions will involve solid, liquid, medical, electronic and hazardous waste. The mission will include matchmaking and company visits, a visit to the recycling fair in Gorinchem, seminars and workshops. Subjects of interest are financing of waste management, waste treatment and recycling of medical, electronic and hazardous waste with specific attention to human health and environment, removal of pathogens from compost, certification processes, marketing approaches and know-how in waste installation and process management.</narrative>
  </description>
